    "long_instructions": "# Make: Design Your Own Generator\r\n\r\n**Your Task:** Write a program that combines at least two string variables into something new and fun. \r\n\r\nYour program must use:\r\n- At least **one concatenation** (`+`)\r\n- At least **one substring** (`[start:end]`)\r\n- *(optional)* a number and `str()` to combine it with a string\r\n\r\n**Challenge:** Use `input()` to assign your variables a value.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1. Fill out **MY PLAN** in `generator_plan.txt` before coding.\r\n2. Write your program according to your plan.\r\n3. Test it with a classmate\r\n4. Fill out the **MY REFLECTION** in `generator_plan.txt`.\r\n\r\n::: details [**Need an idea for your program?**]\r\n\r\n- **Compliment Generator** — combine pieces of someone's name and favorite thing into a made-up compliment\r\n- **License Plate Maker** — build a \"license plate\" from pieces of a name, birth month, and lucky number\r\n- **Superhero Name Creator** — combine a color, an animal, and part of a name into a hero identity\r\n- **Anonymous Username Maker** — build a username using pieces of personal info that a friend couldn't easily trace back to you\r\n:::\r\n",
